      "modelAnswer": "Examination Hall\nNew Delhi - 110001\n\n9th September 2026\n\nThe Editor\nThe Times of India\nBahadur Shah Zafar Marg\nNew Delhi - 110002\n\nSubject: Deep concern regarding the alarming rise in air pollution in Delhi.\n\nRespected Sir/Madam,\n\nThrough the columns of your esteemed newspaper, I wish to draw the attention of the concerned authorities and the general public towards the deteriorating air quality in our national capital, Delhi. The situation has reached a critical stage, posing severe health hazards to every resident.\n\nYear after year, especially during the onset of winter, the Air Quality Index (AQI) breaches the severe category. The toxic smog, primarily caused by unchecked vehicular emissions, rampant construction dust, industrial exhaust, and the burning of agricultural residue in neighboring states, has made breathing a perilous act. Hospitals are reporting a massive surge in patients, particularly children and the elderly, suffering from acute respiratory diseases and asthma.\n\nIt is high time that both the government and the citizens take proactive steps. The authorities must strictly enforce bans on illegal industrial emissions and construction activities during peak pollution days. Furthermore, there must be a massive push to augment public transportation networks and incentivize the adoption of electric vehicles. On a personal level, citizens must adopt carpooling and minimize waste burning.\n\nI hope my letter finds a place in your widely read newspaper so that this grave issue receives the immediate and stringent administrative action it warrants.\n\nThanking you.\n\nYours sincerely,\nXYZ"
